&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=3182676&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=3182676&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We Looking For?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and strategic Compliance &lt;strong&gt;Director of Trust Company and Custody Operations&lt;/strong&gt; to lead and manage regulatory compliance and operational oversight across our trust company, custodial, and trading operations. This individual will play a key role in ensuring compliance with all applicable regulations related to 401(k) plans, ERISA, and trust and custody services. The ideal candidate will bring a deep understanding of regulatory requirements, operational excellence, and a proven track record in managing regulatory operations within financial services or trust company and retirement plan administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Be Doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the regulatory operations function with a focus on &lt;strong&gt;qualified retirement plans&lt;/strong&gt;, particularly &lt;strong&gt;401(k)&lt;/strong&gt; plans, IRAs, and Emergency Savings Accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and implement procedures and internal controls for all trading activities within our custodial operations and proactively monitor our teams and systems for compliance with applicable laws and regulations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with &lt;strong&gt;ERISA&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Internal Revenue Code (IRC)&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;DOL&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;IRS&lt;/strong&gt;, trust company regulations, and &lt;strong&gt;SEC&lt;/strong&gt; regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and enhance controls related to &lt;strong&gt;trust and custody&lt;/strong&gt; operations, as well as &lt;strong&gt;state savings programs&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring alignment with fiduciary standards and regulatory expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular reporting to internal stakeholders and Risk Committee about material risks, incidents, and the effectiveness of risk mitigation strategies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal stakeholders (legal, compliance, product, operations) to interpret new and existing regulations and apply them to business practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor regulatory developments and proactively advise senior leadership on potential business impacts and required changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the lead for&amp;nbsp; the Legal Team to lead the Vestwell Trust Company SOC 1 audit and New Hampshire Banking Department regulatory exam.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with external auditors, regulatory agencies, and third-party service providers during examinations, audits, inquiries, or other matters as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and support regulatory reporting and filings (e.g., Form 5500, IRS/DOL disclosures).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of regulatory operations professionals, providing leadership, coaching, and performance oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement and automation of regulatory and compliance processes and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Necessities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, or a related field required; advanced degree or professional certification (e.g., JD, CPA, CRSP, QKA, CISP) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 10+ years of experience with a proven track record in regulatory compliance or operations in the retirement, trust, or custodial services industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of ERISA, 401(k) regulations, trust company laws, custody services, and applicable IRS/DOL regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing operational risk, compliance audits, and regulatory examinations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and team management skills with the ability to influence and collaborate across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational, analytical, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with recordkeeping platforms, trust accounting systems, or custodial platforms is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Extras&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start up experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role will be based in the New York City office, and will be part of Vestwell&#39;s hybrid in-office operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base salary range for this position is $160K - $180K base. This position is eligible to participate in the Company Bonus Pool and is eligible to receive new hire equity in the Company. Please note that salary bands are based on NY and other similar metro areas and may differ based on where the role is ultimately hired.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Time Employee Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We’re an innovative, high-growth company with an exciting future ahead. At Vestwell, we prioritize employee wellbeing through comprehensive health benefits, generous time off, and a dedicated Employee Wellbeing Committee. Our hybrid work model offers flexibility while providing access to our collaborative offices in Midtown Manhattan, Austin, King of Prussia, and Scottsdale. And, of course, as a company focused on helping people save for the future, we offer a competitive 401(k) plan.&lt;/p&gt;
