&lt;p&gt;Vestwell is expanding and we are looking for someone to join our team. This person must have a passion for data —we’re talking about everything from pipelines to automation to AI. We’re looking for someone who loves to problem-solve and is driven to build great solutions. You will work across all our product lines - translating end-user needs into focused, actionable steps, that result in timely data products. You will help refine and execute our product vision, improving the requirement-intake process, and implementing new processes on a quarterly basis. Vestwell is a continuously evolving data engine at its heart.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role requires someone who dives into whatever challenge is placed in front of them. As a member of the data &amp;amp; analytics squad, you will be involved in the planning, execution, and management of the following facets of our work process: product requirements, functional requirements, acceptance criteria, test cases, AI deep research, and AI tooling. This job requires building a trusted relationship with operations, development, QA, and Vestwell’s business stakeholders to deliver new product features that critically impact the growth of our company and our partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand high-level strategic initiatives and stakeholder requirements; identify opportunities; and translate inputs into buildable features with clear benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively communicate data-based decisions and implementation plans that you will develop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with developers to break down product requirements into discrete tasks with clear functional requirements/acceptance criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist QA team in understanding the appropriate positive and negative test cases to ensure test coverage and a high level of code quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide constant and iterative feedback to the development team, including identifying bugs and assisting in resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete functional testing and provide initial product sign-off when features are ready for end-user verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop processes and tools for tracking usage trends, allowing the data to inform future development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Necessities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional business and systems analysis skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thoroughly understand and document business/functional requirements and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent management of project work through the SDLC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced, project-oriented environment to meet deadlines under tight time constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team environment consisting of Product, Engineering, and QA resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both in verbal and written formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have the ability to interface with internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, must be able to read it and write it to some provable extent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
