&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=3182676&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We Looking For?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Vestwell Government Savings powers state-sponsored savings programs, including 529 college savings, ABLE, child savings accounts, and state auto-IRA programs. We&#39;re building something new for our platform: a full recordkeeping and saver experience for a prepaid tuition 529 program, where families buy tuition credits at today&#39;s rates instead of investing in a portfolio. We&#39;re looking for a hands-on Product Manager who loves solving complex problems and is driven to build great products. This is a greenfield build with a fixed deadline, so you&#39;ll be in the details from day one, working side by side with senior product leads and partners across engineering, QA, design, operations, servicing, relationship management, marketing, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re detail-oriented and structured, and you enjoy getting the details exactly right. You&#39;re curious about how complex systems work, you ask good questions, and you&#39;re comfortable owning your area day to day while knowing when to pull in others. You communicate clearly with engineers, operations, and business stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Be Doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll own defined functional areas of this build, from discovery and requirements through testing and launch, with direction and support from senior product leads. You&#39;ll have your hand in product requirements, functional requirements, acceptance criteria, test cases, and you&#39;ll build strong working relationships with the teams who help get it delivered. This is a great opportunity to go deep on a complex financial product and grow your scope as the program grows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Day-to-Day, You May Also Be Expected To:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the goals and stakeholder needs for your area, and translate them into buildable features with clear intended impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery and write requirements for your features, including business requirements, functional requirements, and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering to break down requirements into stories with clear acceptance criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide constant, iterative feedback to the development team, including identifying bugs and helping resolve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete functional testing and provide product sign-off when features are ready for production release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the senior product leads up to date on progress, risks, and open questions, and bring options when tradeoffs need a decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with operations, servicing, and client teams to make sure what you build works in day-to-day operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to validate assumptions and investigate issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
