&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=3182676&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We Looking For?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vestwell Government Savings powers state-sponsored savings programs, including 529 college savings, ABLE, child savings accounts, and state auto-IRA programs. We&#39;re building something new for our platform: a full recordkeeping and saver experience for a prepaid tuition 529 program, where families buy tuition credits at today&#39;s rates instead of investing in a portfolio.&amp;nbsp;We&#39;re looking for an experienced, hands-on Senior Product Manager who loves solving complex problems and can own large, ambiguous areas with minimal direction. This is a greenfield build with a fixed deadline, so you&#39;ll be in the details from day one, working side by side with a delivery lead PM and partners across engineering, QA, design, operations, servicing, relationship management, marketing, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;re a systems thinker who enjoys problems where the details have to be exactly right. You&#39;re comfortable owning an area with some ambiguity, you ask hard questions early, and you can explain complex topics clearly to engineers, operations, and clients alike. You&#39;ve owned large, cross-functional initiatives before and know how to keep a complex build moving when the path isn&#39;t clear.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Be Doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll own the most complex functional areas of this build end to end, from discovery and requirements through testing and launch, and you&#39;ll be one of the people on the team who knows exactly how the system should behave. You&#39;ll have your hand in product requirements, functional requirements, acceptance criteria, test cases, and you&#39;ll need strong relationships with operations, engineering, QA, and business stakeholders to get it delivered. You&#39;ll also help set the bar for how product work is done on the team, guiding other PMs and acting as a go-to product voice for internal teams, clients, and partners.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Day-to-Day, You May Also Be Expected To:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand program goals and stakeholder needs, and translate them into buildable features with clear intended impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own discovery and requirements for your functional areas, including business requirements, functional requirements, and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering to break down requirements into stories with clear acceptance criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide constant, iterative feedback to the development team, including identifying bugs and helping resolve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete functional testing and provide product sign-off when features are ready for production release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside the delivery lead PM to keep scope, dependencies, and risks visible across squads, and make tradeoff decisions as new information comes in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with operations, client teams, and external partners to make sure what we build works in day-to-day operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to validate assumptions, investigate issues, and inform product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery for ambiguous, high-risk areas, framing options and tradeoffs for leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and guide other PMs on the team, reviewing requirements and raising the quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent product with clients and external partners, and drive alignment across teams without needing escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Necessities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Product Management experience, including owning a large, cross-functional initiative end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building complex financial or transaction-based systems (e.g., recordkeeping, payments, ledgers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional business and systems analysis skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thoroughly understand and document business/functional requirements and business use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving the software development lifecycle in an Agile environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced, project-oriented environment and meet deadlines under tight time constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively across Product, Engineering, QA, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interface with internal stakeholders, executives, and external clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL and data integrations (e.g., APIs, JSON, XML, file-based integrations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
