&lt;p&gt;We’re growing our Employer Service team and adding a Training Manager to own the full training ecosystem for the specialists who serve 401(k) plan sponsors, HR and payroll administrators, and partners such as TPAs and advisers. You’re a proactive, organized leader and skilled facilitator who can turn complex retirement plan concepts into clear, practical learning that gets new hires productive quickly and keeps the whole team sharp as our products and regulations evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role partners closely with Employer Service leadership, Plan Onboarding, Operations, Compliance, and product teams to make sure our team is confident, knowledgeable, and ready to deliver an excellent employer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Be Doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day-to-Day, You Will Be Expected To:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead New-Hire Onboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the new-hire training program for Employer Service specialists, from day one through full proficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver engaging instructor-led, virtual, and hands-on training sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design nesting and shadowing plans that move new hires from classroom to live work with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess readiness through knowledge checks and practical exercises before new hires take on full workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build Curriculum &amp;amp; Content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training on 401(k) plan fundamentals, including eligibility, vesting, contributions and match, loans, distributions, and payroll integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create training on employer-facing workflows such as plan onboarding, payroll file issues, plan feature changes, and partner support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain training materials, procedures, job aids, knowledge-base articles, and learning paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep all content accurate, current, and aligned with company policy and applicable ERISA, DOL, and IRS requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Drive Ongoing Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver refresher training for new processes, product releases, plan design changes, and regulatory updates (e.g., SECURE 2.0 provisions).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build advanced and specialized learning paths that support career growth and cross-training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a training calendar that balances team development with service-level needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure Training Effectiveness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track training completion, assessment results, time to proficiency**, [e.g., against a target of X weeks]**, and post-training performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather feedback from learners and leaders to continuously improve content and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on training impact to leadership and recommend improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance and quality trends shared by supervisors to identify where targeted training is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Partner Across the Organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with supervisors and managers to understand skill gaps and team needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and engineering to prepare the team ahead of new feature and system releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Compliance to ensure required regulatory and data-security training is delivered and documented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold strict confidentiality and data-protection standards in all training materials and examples.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Necessities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience leading training or learning and development in a retirement plan, recordkeeping, financial services, or client service environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of 401(k) plan administration, including contributions, loans, distributions, and payroll processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong facilitation and presentation skills, both in person and virtually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing training content; familiarity with instructional design and LMS tools is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working familiarity with ERISA and DOL/IRS requirements; industry designations (e.g., QKA, CRPS) are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to service excellence and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in either the New York City, Austin, King of Prussia, or Scottsdale office, and will be part of Vestwell&#39;s hybrid in-office operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base salary range for this position is $80K - $95K base. This position is eligible to participate in the Company Bonus Pool and is eligible to receive new hire equity in the Company. Please note that salary bands are based on NY and other similar metro areas and may differ based on where the role is ultimately hired.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Time Employee Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We’re an innovative, high-growth company with an exciting future ahead. At Vestwell, we prioritize employee wellbeing through comprehensive health benefits, generous time off, and a dedicated Employee Wellbeing Committee. Our hybrid work model offers flexibility while providing access to our collaborative offices in Midtown Manhattan, Austin, King of Prussia, and Scottsdale. And, of course, as a company focused on helping people save for the future, we offer a competitive 401(k) plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our interview process starts the same for every candidate with 1-2 introductory conversations to learn more about your background, interests, and what you&#39;re looking for, while also giving you the opportunity to learn more about Vestwell and the team. From there, the process varies by role but typically includes a skills or experience-based assessment, such as a coding interview, portfolio review, or deeper discussion of your relevant experience. Successful candidates then move on to a virtual or in-person interview panel. Before extending an offer, we complete a reference check with a current or former manager and a peer. Throughout the process, we prioritize transparency, clear communication, and minimizing surprises.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For your awareness you will only receive correspondence from &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting@vestwell.com&quot;&gt;recruiting@vestwell.com&lt;/a&gt; any other domain not ending in&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://vestwell.com/&quot;&gt;vestwell.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;is not our Recruitment team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vestwell’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vestwell.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;Attention California residents: In the course of conducting our business and complying with federal, state, and local government regulations governing such matters as employment, tax, insurance, etc., we must collect Personal Information from you. Should you accept employment with Vestwell you may view our California Privacy Rights Act here:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lKSzA8qE7YIAJe2ZZahLWzFp9EZP1IuS/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=111643980444675168924&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vestwell’s California Privacy Rights Policy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vestwell is the financial technology company powering the new savings economy. The New York City-based fintech platform redefines how people save for the critical aspects of life across retirement, education, and healthcare savings needs. Today, Vestwell enables over 790,000 businesses and more than 2.75 million active savers, with over $57 billion in assets saved across all 50 United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vestwell offers a range of products, including workplace-delivered retirement plans, employer-offered student loan repayment benefits, and various savings accounts for education, emergencies, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vestwell&#39;s platform serves a diverse clientele, including financial advisers, employers, third-party administrators, financial institutions, payroll providers, government agencies, and individual savers. To learn more, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://vestwell.com/&quot;&gt;vestwell.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=3182676&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=3182676&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We Looking For?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We&#39;re growing our Employer Service team and adding a Workforce Manager to own how we forecast, staff, schedule, and manage in real time.&amp;nbsp; Our team supports 401(k) plan sponsors, payroll administrators, and partners across phone, email, and case queues. The ideal candidate is an analytical, detail-oriented planner who can balance service levels, staff utilization, and employee experience, and who understands the seasonal rhythms of the retirement plan business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an analytical, detail-oriented planner who can balance service levels, staff utilization, and employee experience, and you understand the seasonal rhythms of the retirement plan business. You’ll partner closely with Employer Service leadership to make sure we have the right people, with the right skills, in the right place at the right time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Be Doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day-to-Day, You Will Be Expected To:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Forecasting &amp;amp; Capacity Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain short- and long-term forecasts for call, email, and case volume and handle time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model staffing needs and hiring plans in partnership with leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account for 401(k) seasonality and event-driven spikes, such as plan onboarding waves, plan conversions, year-end, compliance testing, and Form 5500 season.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update forecasts as business drivers change, including new partner launches and product releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Manage Scheduling &amp;amp; Real-Time Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build schedules that meet service-level goals while balancing training, QA, coaching, and time-off needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor queues intraday and adjust staffing, breaks, and work assignments to protect service levels and case SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage skill-based routing and queue prioritization across phone, email, and case work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate time-off, overtime, and shrinkage planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Drive Reporting &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own WFM reporting, including service level, ASA, abandon rate, occupancy, adherence, shrinkage, and case backlog and aging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present trends and staffing recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure forecast accuracy against [target, e.g., X% at the interval or weekly level],&amp;nbsp; and continuously refine models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Optimize Tools &amp;amp; Processes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer WFM and case management tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document WFM policies and procedures, including adherence and time-off standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify automation and process opportunities that reduce manual work and improve efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold strict confidentiality and data-protection standards when working with plan sponsor and participant data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Necessities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Experience in workforce management, forecasting, or capacity planning in a contact center or service environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multichannel queues (phone, email, case/ticket)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills; advanced Excel and hands-on experience with WFM tools and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to present data-driven recommendations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of 401(k) or retirement plan services is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to service excellence and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Extras&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of 401(k) or retirement plan services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
